# ============================================================
# SEARCH HISTORY API TESTING GUIDE
# Base URL: http://localhost:7410/api/user/search-history
# ============================================================

# ----- STEP 1: Login and paste your token below -----
@baseUrl     = http://localhost:7410/api/user/search-history
@token       = PASTE_YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

# ----- REAL IDs (fill after each step) -----
@searchHistoryId = PASTE_SEARCH_HISTORY_ITEM_ID_HERE

# ============================================================
# 1. SAVE / TRACK SEARCH QUERY
# ============================================================

### 1.1 Save a new search query (or update count if exists)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "saree"
}

###

### 1.2 Save another search query
POST {{baseUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "cotton silk saree"
}

###

### 1.3 Update the count of an existing query (run 1.1 again to test increment)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "saree"
}

###

# ============================================================
# 2. FETCH SEARCH HISTORIES & TRENDS
# ============================================================

### 2.1 Get Recent Searches for Logged-in User
# Should return the most recently searched items first
GET {{baseUrl}}?limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 2.2 Get Globally Trending Searches
# Aggregates searches across all users and returns highest count first
GET {{baseUrl}}/trending?limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 2.3 Get Quick Search Suggestions
# Useful for autocomplete: finds existing queries matching the 'q' parameter
GET {{baseUrl}}/suggestions?q=saree&limit=5
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

# ============================================================
# 3. DELETE SEARCH HISTORY
# ============================================================

### 3.1 Delete a specific search history item
# Requires: @searchHistoryId to be set at top (copy from 2.1 response)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/{{searchHistoryId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 3.2 Clear ALL search history for the logged-in user
DELETE {{baseUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}



